            <div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-body field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><h3><strong>Wet Felting: Lantern Workshop with Ann McElroy</strong></h3>
<p>Saturday, August 22 from 1 pm to 5 pm<br>Ages 16 and up<br>Cost: $80.75 plus tax<br><a href="https://anc.ca.apm.activecommunities.com/ottawa/activity/search/detail/195166?onlineSiteId=0&amp;locale=en-US&amp;from_original_cui=true">Advance registration is required.&nbsp;</a></p>
<p>Learn the art of felt making in a unique heritage setting at Pinhey's Point Historic Site. Led by Ann from <a href="https://shepherdsspringfarm.ca/">Shepherds' Spring Farm</a>, you will create a thin, translucent cover for a glass lantern filled with fairly lights. Once felted, the cover will glow beautifully from within. This workshop requires no sewing and is beginner friendly. Using loose fluffy wool, silk, and other fibers, participants will create a lantern cover that looks beautiful both with and without the lights on. All materials are included in the cost of registration, including the glass lantern and the fairy lights. The project will be completed during the workshop; however, participants will receive instructions to inspire future projects at home. Light refreshments will be served.</p>
<h4>Notes</h4>
<ul>
<li>This workshop is delivered in English.</li>
<li>Advance registration is required. Workshops with insufficient registration may be cancelled. If an alternative cannot be offered, a refund will be issued.</li>
<li>Visit the <a href="https://ottawa.ca/en/recreation-and-parks/register-courses-and-camps/registration-terms-and-cancellations/financial-support-ottawa-hand-hand">Ottawa Hand in Hand</a> web page for information on available financial supports to facilitate participation in recreation and culture programs.</li>
<li>This workshop is hosted indoors on the ground level of the heritage house at Pinhey's Point. There is a gravel pathway from the parking lot to the house, and two accessible parking spaces are located in the parking lot closest to the museum. Additional <a href="https://ottawa.ca/en/recreation-and-parks/facilities/place-listing/pinheys-point-historic-site-0#section-17489d56-6b33-4d66-a044-ec61844387c4">information about accessibility</a> can be found on the museum webpage. If you have questions or concerns regarding accessibility, please contact the museum by email at <a href="mailto:museums@ottawa.ca">museums@ottawa.ca</a>.<br>&nbsp;</li>
