<p>Date: Saturday, October 10<br>Time: 10 am to 12:30 pm<br>Fee: $26.75 plus tax<br>Ages 14 and up<br><a href="https://anc.ca.apm.activecommunities.com/ottawa/activity/search/detail/195169?onlineSiteId=0&amp;locale=en-US&amp;from_original_cui=true"><strong>Advance registration is required.&nbsp;</strong></a></p>
<p>Join environmental educator <a href="https://cliffland.ca/visiting/workshops/chad-clifford/">Chad Clifford</a> at Pinhey’s Point as he draws on more than three decades of experience teaching natural history and wilderness skills. Explore the site on a guided walk to learn all about its natural features and history, while picking up some basic wilderness survival skills along the way.&nbsp;</p>
